Original commit body from 0ed6a63ec5a6eca8a3e2a916178182d346476492:

validate_pass_dependencies was a pre-run CNF gate that raised. ADR-0056 W1
refused to wire it, because raising is the withholding direction and 29.2% of
surveys carry a falsified declaration, and it was kept only so its 11 tests
stayed green. Nothing called it outside those tests. Measured on a one-.js,
one-.rs Tauri fixture, it would have raised on 12 of 71 active passes, every one
a repo-lacks-the-language case; run over the full catalog it can never fail.
Three wired mechanisms already do its jobs: name resolution in CI,
prerequisite_absent at the linker chokepoint, and the post-run falsification
audit.

Removed: the function, its 11 tests, its test-only-reachability baseline key.
ADR-0030 no longer says dependencies are checked at configuration time.
ADR-0056 W1 is edited in place, and its pass-level-selector trigger now names
a disclosure, not a raise, as the answer.

Added, the two static checks it never made:
- validate_pass_name_resolution refuses an empty inner clause ([[]], an OR of
  nothing). An outer [] stays legal. The runtime readers disagreed about [[]],
  and no live declaration has one.
- TestLinkerDependenciesRunEarlier: a linker named in another linker's
  depends_on sits in a STRICTLY lower priority group, because same-priority
  linkers run in parallel from one snapshot. The three such pairs all hold
  today. A floor and two mutation controls (same priority, later priority) show
  it can fail.

No output, schema or governance change. Addresses WI-rihob; INV-hujog stays
violated on WI-nijil and the WI-rasal family.

